# TraceHealth — Environment Variables

## Backend (backend/.env)

```env
# ── MongoDB (Atlas M0 free tier) ──────────────────────────────────────────────
MONGO_URI=mongodb+srv://<user>:<password>@<cluster>.mongodb.net/healthrisk
MONGO_DB_NAME=healthrisk

# ── JWT — sign/verify all tokens locally (no external auth service) ───────────
# Generate with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('base64'))"
JWT_SECRET=replace-with-a-long-random-secret
JWT_ALGORITHM=HS256
ACCESS_TOKEN_EXPIRE_MINUTES=60
REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRE_DAYS=30

# ── Admin account (created via POST /api/auth/admin/setup) ───────────────────
ADMIN_EMAIL=admin@yourdomain.com
ADMIN_PASSWORD=replace-with-a-strong-password

# ── Google OAuth (optional — leave blank to disable the Google button) ────────
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:8000/api/auth/google/callback

# ── CORS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
# Comma-separated additional origins (e.g., staging URLs)
EXTRA_ALLOWED_ORIGINS=

# ── App ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
ENVIRONMENT=development    # "development" | "production"

# ── ML model artifacts path (relative to backend/ directory) ─────────────────
MODELS_DIR=../models       # use /app/models inside Docker
```

## Frontend (frontend/.env)

```env
# URL of the FastAPI backend (no trailing slash)
VITE_API_BASE_URL=http://localhost:8000
```

## Docker Compose root environment

When using `docker compose up`, you can pass the following env vars at the shell level:

```env
# Public backend URL — embedded in the React build
VITE_API_BASE_URL=https://your-render-service.onrender.com
```

## Notes

- Never commit `.env` files to git. They are listed in `.gitignore`.
- In production (Render), set all backend variables via the Render dashboard **Environment** section.
- In production (Vercel), set `VITE_API_BASE_URL` via the Vercel **Environment Variables** section.
- `JWT_SECRET` must be a long (48+ byte), cryptographically random string. Rotate it to invalidate all existing sessions.
- `ADMIN_EMAIL` / `ADMIN_PASSWORD` are only used once during the one-time `POST /api/auth/admin/setup` call. After that, you can remove them from the env if desired.
